# Battery and reminders

Battery life on older devices is a **feature**, not an afterthought.

## Do

- Schedule notifications with platform-appropriate APIs; reschedule after boot (`RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED` only if needed)
- Use **exact alarms** only when the user expects a precise reminder; gate behind the system permission UX on modern Android
- Collapse / debounce bursts so one morning doesn’t fire ten separate wakes if tasks can share a digest (product may choose per-task vs digest — document choice in `docs/`)
- Test reminder behavior under Doze / battery optimization; document OEM gotchas
- Prefer one short-lived wake to do work, then release

## Do not

- Run a sticky foreground service for “better engagement”
- Poll in a loop or use high-frequency `WorkManager` periods
- Hold wake locks across UI sessions
- Sync or network in the background by default

## Reminder UX

- Notification actions: at least **Done** and **Snooze** when practical
- Missing a reminder must not corrupt cadence math — define behavior in architecture docs
